@host = localhost:8080
@user_id = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@service_id = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

# ─── Ops ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Health Check

GET {{host}}/health

### Swagger UI

GET {{host}}/swagger/index.html

### System Stats (hardcoded mock data)

GET {{host}}/api/system/stats

### Legacy Services (hardcoded mock data)

GET {{host}}/api/legacy/services


# ─── Auth ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Session is cookie-based (HttpOnly `session_token` set on login).
# Send cookies with requests (VS Code REST Client: enable "Send cookies").

### Register (role forced to `user`)

POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Login

POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "remember_me": true
}

### Login as Demo (seeded guest user, no body)

POST {{host}}/api/auth/demo

### Logout (works anonymously, clears cookie)

POST {{host}}/api/auth/logout

### Get Current User (401 without valid session)

GET {{host}}/api/auth/me


# ─── Users ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# {id} = UUID. Path param is `{id}`, not `{user_id}`.
# List/create/delete are admin-session-only. Self-registration lives at
# POST /api/auth/register (role forced to `user`).
# Native routes also accept `Authorization: Bearer <api-key>` (key acts as
# its owner): self-reads and /me need identity only; list/create/delete
# and key management need the `admin` key scope; other-user reads need
# `admin` scope too (403 otherwise, even for admin-owned read keys).

### List Users (admin session or admin-scoped key; 401 anonymous, 403 non-admin)

GET {{host}}/api/users

### List Users with write-only API key (expect 403, leaks nothing)

GET {{host}}/api/users
Authorization: Bearer cgw_live_PASTE_WRITE_KEY_HERE

### Create User (admin session; role from body trusted — admins only)

POST {{host}}/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "newuser@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "role": "user"
}

### Get User (session or key; 403 unless admin-or-self; key needs admin scope for other users)

GET {{host}}/api/users/{{user_id}}

### Get Other User with admin-owned read API key (expect 403 — no admin scope)

GET {{host}}/api/users/{{user_id}}
Authorization: Bearer cgw_live_PASTE_ADMIN_READ_KEY_HERE

### Update User (session required; admin or self; role change requires admin)

PUT {{host}}/api/users/{{user_id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "updated@example.com"
}

### Update User Password

PUT {{host}}/api/users/{{user_id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "password": "newpassword123"
}

### Delete User (admin session; cannot delete self or demo@example.com; 204)

DELETE {{host}}/api/users/{{user_id}}

### Get Self with API key (any owned key; 200)

GET {{host}}/api/users/{{user_id}}
Authorization: Bearer cgw_live_PASTE_USER_KEY_HERE

### Create User with low-scope API key (expect 403, creates nothing)

POST {{host}}/api/users
Authorization: Bearer cgw_live_PASTE_READ_KEY_HERE
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nope@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "role": "user"
}

### Create User with admin API key (201)

POST {{host}}/api/users
Authorization: Bearer cgw_live_PASTE_ADMIN_KEY_HERE
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "newuser@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "role": "user"
}


# ─── Services (monitor) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# {id} = UUID. All routes are admin-session-only (401 anonymous, 403 non-admin).

### Create Service (defaults: interval 60, method GET, timeout 5000, codes [200,204])

POST {{host}}/api/services
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "My Service",
  "url": "https://example.com",
  "icon": "🚀",
  "description": "A test service",
  "service_type": "web",
  "health_check_interval": 60,
  "health_check_method": "GET",
  "expected_status_codes": [200],
  "timeout": 5000
}

### List Services

GET {{host}}/api/services/list

### Get All Services Stats

GET {{host}}/api/services/stats/all

### Get Service

GET {{host}}/api/services/{{service_id}}

### Update Service (partial; all fields optional)

PUT {{host}}/api/services/{{service_id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Updated Service",
  "is_active": false
}

### Delete Service (204)

DELETE {{host}}/api/services/{{service_id}}

### Get Service History (limit hardcoded to 100)

GET {{host}}/api/services/{{service_id}}/history

### Get Service Stats (24h / 7d / 30d uptime)

GET {{host}}/api/services/{{service_id}}/stats


# ─── API Keys (session + admin) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Owned keys only (owner = caller). Plaintext is returned exactly once
# by Create; List never exposes secrets. Valid scopes: "admin",
# "<service>:read|write|admin" (e.g. "corefinance:read"). Unknown
# scopes → 400. An admin key is scopes=["admin"] with no expiry.
# Key-authed callers may only mint scopes they hold (`admin` presenter
# may mint anything); low-scope mint of unheld scope → 403.

### Create API Key

POST {{host}}/api/auth/keys
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "label": "ops-script",
  "scopes": ["corefinance:read"]
}

### Create Admin API Key (admin session; never expires)

POST {{host}}/api/auth/keys
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "label": "ops-admin",
  "scopes": ["admin"]
}

### List API Keys (admin session or admin-scoped key; write-only key → 403)

GET {{host}}/api/auth/keys

### List API Keys with write-only API key (expect 403, leaks nothing)

GET {{host}}/api/auth/keys
Authorization: Bearer cgw_live_PASTE_WRITE_KEY_HERE

### Revoke API Key (immediate effect; 204)

DELETE {{host}}/api/auth/keys/{{key_id}}

### Mint with admin API key (key acts as owner; 201 + one-time plaintext)

POST {{host}}/api/auth/keys
Authorization: Bearer cgw_live_PASTE_ADMIN_KEY_HERE
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "label": "script-key",
  "scopes": ["corefinance:read"]
}


# ─── Budget (reverse-proxied to corefinance) ─────────────────────────────────
# Any method/subpath under /api/budget/** is proxied to COREFINANCE_URL.
# The edge authenticates (session cookie OR API key), creates a short-lived
# internal JWT, and forwards it as Authorization: Bearer. No session and no
# key → 401, never proxied. X-User-ID is never accepted downstream.
# Key callers need service cover: GET/HEAD needs `<svc>:read` cover,
# writes need `<svc>:write` cover (`admin` and `<svc>:admin` pass both);
# sessions pass through. Uncovered keys → 403, never proxied.
# Full endpoint list: services/corefinance/budget-api.http

### Priority Groups (public downstream; via gateway still needs edge identity)

GET {{host}}/api/budget/priority-groups

### Expense Categories (requires session)

GET {{host}}/api/budget/expense-categories/

### Income Categories (requires session)

GET {{host}}/api/budget/incomes/

### Budget Remaining (requires session)

GET {{host}}/api/budget/remaining

### Budget Remaining targeted (admin session; edge validates ?user_id=)

GET {{host}}/api/budget/remaining?user_id=PASTE_TARGET_USER_UUID_HERE

### Budget targeted with malformed user_id (expect 400)

GET {{host}}/api/budget/remaining?user_id=zzz

### Budget targeted as non-admin (expect 403)

GET {{host}}/api/budget/remaining?user_id=PASTE_OTHER_USER_UUID_HERE

### Stats Summary (requires session)

GET {{host}}/api/budget/stats/summary?start_date=2026-09-01&end_date=2026-09-30

### Export Budget (requires session)

GET {{host}}/api/budget/export

### Budget with API key instead of cookie (edge validates, creates, proxies)

GET {{host}}/api/budget/remaining
Authorization: Bearer cgw_live_PASTE_USER_KEY_HERE

### Budget GET with write-only API key (expect 403, never proxied)

GET {{host}}/api/budget/remaining
Authorization: Bearer cgw_live_PASTE_WRITE_KEY_HERE

### Budget POST with read-only API key (expect 403, never proxied)

POST {{host}}/api/budget/expenses
Authorization: Bearer cgw_live_PASTE_READ_KEY_HERE
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 1
}

### Budget without credentials (expect 401, never proxied)

GET {{host}}/api/budget/remaining

### Admin path without admin scope (expect 403)

POST {{host}}/api/budget/admin/backfill?dry_run=true

### Admin backfill dry-run (admin session, expect counts, no mutation)

POST {{host}}/api/budget/admin/backfill?dry_run=true

### Admin backfill execute for another user (admin session)

POST {{host}}/api/budget/admin/backfill?user_id=PASTE_TARGET_USER_UUID_HERE

